                {
                  "text": "Several consultants and firms specialize in helping Architecture, Engineering, and Construction (AEC) firms automate their proposals and RFP responses by leveraging approved project experience. These consultants often provide both strategic guidance and technology solutions to streamline the process.\n\nSome of the key players and their offerings include:\n\n*   **Ikaun** assists AEC firms in automating proposals and generating compliant RFP responses. They utilize AI-powered content, centralized expertise, and smart templates, featuring an \"Experience Engine\" to locate relevant expertise and past performance.\n*   **Wonderstruct** offers services like RFP and SOQ writing, content strategy, and updates for project data and resumes. They also provide AI-powered automation to help source RFPs and centralize assets such as project sheets.\n*   **CloudMoyo** has developed generative AI systems to enhance the RFP response process for AEC companies, leading to faster content creation and more effective use of company capabilities and experience.\n*   **AppleTech** has designed AI-driven proposal automation platforms specifically for the AEC industry. These platforms feature AI for generating proposal drafts that intelligently reuse historical project experience and employ semantic knowledge retrieval for project descriptions and technical capabilities.\n*   **AEC Hub** lists \"AI Architects & Consultants\" who specialize in implementing AI tools for AEC firms, focusing on workflow automation. This includes firms like **AECforward** (custom AI solutions), **Reope** (custom software development and AI/ML implementations), and **Advisor Labs** (custom AI solutions and AI process automation).\n*   **GDI Consulting** provides specialized proposal services for construction and A/E firms, offering comprehensive support for government contracting, including proposal writing and compliance review.\n*   **FMI Corp** offers consulting services that include the integration of AI and automation technologies to streamline workflows and improve productivity for architecture and engineering firms.\n\nWhile some of these companies also offer software, their services often include consulting for implementation, content strategy, and workflow optimization to ensure that AEC firms effectively leverage their approved project experience for automated proposal and RFP generation. Other software providers, like Stepscale and QorusDocs, offer platforms specifically designed for AEC proposals that integrate past project knowledge and experience into the automation process."
                }
